id: pm-vcs-ijj7
title: "Phase 2: change identities and history rewriting"
description: "A version control system that cannot rewrite history is a snapshot store. This phase gives every commit a change identity that survives rewriting, and adds describe, rebase, squash, split, cherry-pick, revert, reset and restore. Descendants are replayed automatically and every branch and tag pointing into a rewritten range is moved, so a rewrite can never orphan a ref. Every rewrite is one transactional operation-log entry, so undo reverses it whole."
type: Epic
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:28:23.482Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-31T12:05:54.664Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-31T12:05:54.646Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-31T12:05:54.646Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 540
acceptance_criteria: "Every commit carries a change id that is preserved across describe, rebase, squash and split; rewriting a commit with descendants replays all of them and moves every affected branch and tag; a conflicting rewrite changes no ref and no working-tree byte; record paths merge per field during replay, never by line; 100 percent line, branch and function coverage"
resolution: "Delivered persistent change identities and describe, rebase, squash, split, cherry-pick, revert, reset, restore, and show with descendant replay, affected-ref movement, conflict atomicity, record-field convergence, and operation-log undo."
expected_result: Every Phase 2 acceptance criterion is proven through real engine and host command tests with exact 100 percent source coverage.
actual_result: "Nine child tasks and their feature are closed with verb-specific evidence; 342 tests and installed npm/Bun probes pass; exact line, branch, and function coverage is 100 percent."
