notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T08:32:27.060Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation and command surface complete: engine/rewrite.ts plus nine verbs (describe, rebase, squash, split, cherry-pick, revert, reset, restore, show) and log --change-ids. 337 tests pass. Change identities survive describe, rebase, squash and split; a cherry-pick deliberately gets a NEW id because it is a second distinct change; descendants are replayed and every branch and tag pointing into a rewritten range moves with it; a conflicting rewrite refuses having changed no ref and no working-tree byte, proven by asserting both refs and the file contents after a forced conflict. Four review-quality fixes made on top of what was generated: the six duplicated conflict-translation arms became one shared planned() helper, because four of the six operations cannot conflict at all and six copies read as though every operation can; topoSort became an iterative depth-first walk with push-time dedupe, replacing a scan-for-progress loop whose no-progress guard was unreachable; an empty split half now reports empty_split instead of being dressed up as a conflict whose remediation told the caller to resolve paths that matched nothing; and the rebase replay threads its previous parent through a variable instead of reading it back out of a list with an unreachable fallback."
close_reason: Phase 2 change identities and transactional history rewriting completed
